@template brisk
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- Yesterday's shirt. Wardrobe, then carry on.
- Same clothes as yesterday. Noted. Change when you can.
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- Fresh shirt tomorrow. You'll feel sharper. Promise.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- Grime on the sleeve. Change before your next job.
- That uniform's done a shift. Two, by the look.   #funny
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- Good work, by the state of you. Now go and change.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- {hi}. Quick one? I've got five minutes.
- {hi}. Good timing. I was about to move on.
- {hi}, {nick}. Keep it short and I'm all yours.
- Right. You. What's the news?
- {hi}. All well with you? Good.
- {hi}. Something I can do for you?
- {hi}. You look like you've got a question.
- On my way somewhere. Walk with me a minute.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Good to see a face that gets things done.
- {hi}. Heard your last job went well. Noted.
? time:morning
- Morning. Day's started. Let's get on with it.
? time:evening
- Evening. Done for the day? Me nearly.
== near
- Busy here. Talk while I work?
- This bit won't take long. Then I'm free.
- {room}. Everything in its place. Mostly.
- Half done. The other half's the hard half.
- Hand me that? No, the other one. Thanks.
- Working down the list. Three left.
- Nearly there. Give me a minute.
- Good. You're here. Hold this.
